Ethics Statement




This paper proposes a method for amortizing long-form reasoning traces into query-conditioned parameter updates, improving the efficiency of LLM inference on mathematical reasoning tasks. While this work is motivated by reducing computational cost in settings such as math problem solving, efficiency improvements to LLM reasoning could, in principle, lower the barrier to deploying reasoning models for harmful purposes. This concern is not unique to our approach but applies broadly to research that improves the cost-performance tradeoff of LLM inference.








