2610.03021v1,Small universal multiset reaction systems,"In living cells, molecular species are typically present in multiple copies, and their abundance plays a decisive role in determining whether reactions occur and at what rate. The assumption that an entity is either present or absent ignores the influence of concentration on system dynamics and prevents the description of many important biological phenomena, including threshold effects, competition for limited resources, and stochastic fluctuations arising from finite molecular populations.","5 
Conclusions




We introduced the implementation of a small universal machine of 23 instructions using multiset reactions systems.
We encoded the registers and instructions labels as specific elements.
We have shown that all types of instructions can be modeled using reaction chains.
Reactions chains that model a specific instruction can only be enabled once the element encoding the instruction label is generated, ensuring that instructions are executed sequentially.






