itself capture the frequency decorrelation of dust emission. Follow-up work will address these by predicting per-pixel uncertainties under a Gaussian negative log-likelihood, exploiting Planck half-mission splits to decouple the target noise from the sky signal, and extending the framework to predict multiple frequencies jointly.










We will make the dust ViT model discussed in this work, in addition to the high-resolution 353 GHz polarization maps, publicly available upon publication.




