In our formal problem statement of SPSE Definition 9 the ansatz Hamiltonian is only free on
a subset of modes and allows for a spectator HamiltonianHO. The contour integration used by
SPICES can exclude roots outside of the chosen contour, including roots introduced by spectator
modes. We discuss in Section 7 how the SPICES protocol behaves in this setting, and when it can
robustly retrieve the free roots.
