The requirement that the spectator roots lie outside of the energy annulus is included so that the
problem has a unique solution, and it is also motivated by the feature of SPICES that roots outside
of the annulus are not included in the signal. WhenHO is itself free, condition (ii) says exactly
that no single-particle energy ofHO lies inΩ, and in this case it holds for all timest. WhenHO is
interacting there is no notion of single-particle energies for the spectator sector, and (ii) serves as
the natural generalization of this free condition.
