factor and an interacting spectator factor. If the spectator factor has no zeros in the target annulus,
then its contribution to the annular root moment vanishes exactly, regardless of the size of the
perturbation. The magnitude of the perturbation enters only when trying to ensure that the annulus
remains free of zeros from the interacting sector and in the numerical conditioning of the contour
estimator. Proofs of the supporting statements are again in Section A.
