8.1 DQC1 hardness of protected-energy recovery
We now show that the task of Definition 43, which is the single-atom special case of Definition 9, is
DQC1-hard.
Definition 43(Operational protected-energy recovery).The input is an operational description
in the sense of Definition 10, together with a target intervalΩ. It is promised that the protected
measure inΩis a single atomδ E⋆. A valid output is either:
1. a polynomial-bit rationalbEsatisfying| bE−E ⋆|<1/2; or
2. a finitely represented probability measurebνwhose first moment is approximable in deterministic
polynomial time to additive error1/12, and which satisfies
W1(bν,δE⋆)≤ 1
3.
The solver must succeed with probability at least2/3, with total classical running time and elementary-
gate count polynomial in the input length on every execution. These costs include compilation
