guarantees hold with an external control.
Proof. Standard phase estimation (see, e.g., [36, Sec. 5.2]) estimates an eigenphase to accuracy
∆/4with probability at least3/4, usingO(∆−1)controlled queries. The boundary-gap assumption
therefore gives the correct membership bit with the same probability. We can then repeat phase
estimation O(log(1/η))times, and then compute the majority bit to reduce the error probability to
p≤η 2/16.
Finally, we copy the output bit into a fresh qubit and uncompute all work registers. The standard
compute-copy-uncompute bound (see, e.g., [40, Theorem 4.14]) gives norm error at most2√p≤η/ 2.
Allowing total gate-synthesis errorη/2gives the claimed error and query complexity.
This filter is the only quantum subroutine we need to implement the projectors that defineW.
The next lemma uses it to compileWitself.
