(
Burda et al., 2019b
; 
Burda et al., 2019a
)
: in the pendulum systems the agent can accumulate reward by spinning freely, and in the hopper by uncontrolled thrashing. Adding joint damping removed these optima in our environments: damping taxes indiscriminate velocity accumulation while leaving configuration-dependent instability rewarded. However, this is an environment-level modification rather than an objective-level one, and a principled resolution remains open.






Each limitation suggests future work. Jacobians can in principle be extracted from a learned world model: one-step forward models of the kind trained by curiosity methods 
(
Pathak et al., 2017
)
 are differentiable by construction, which would make F-CIP fully learning-based and simulator-agnostic. The 
