not make all available context useful.
29
Askour & Merimi  ·  The Context-Sufficiency Frontier in Generative AI Personalization
The experiment shows why the distinction matters. Relevant context improved personalization. 
Irrelevant  context  reduced  appropriateness  and  stability.  Additional  context  could  alter  
retrieval  even  when  the  final  recommendations  remained  broadly  consistent  with  the  
customer’s request, and one provider-goal signal carried products through a process that the  
provider’s own rule was intended to exclude. A 50-case cross-model check using GPT Astra 6  
produced the same directional pattern, suggesting that the central relevance result is not  
confined to the open-weights model used for the full experiment.
The theoretical implication is therefore not that personalization systems need more context.  
They need sufficient context. The Context-Sufficiency Frontier identifies the point at which  
the  relevant  circumstances  of  the  decision  have  been  adequately  covered  and  additional 
information stops creating value. The decision context package translates that idea into a  
managerial  unit:  provide  what  this  interaction  needs,  enforce  the  applicable  constraints  
throughout the process, and do not treat information as useful merely because it is available.  
For service research, the broader lesson is that moving personalization into generative systems  
transfers situational judgment only when the provider also transfers its selection.",cues
