2.3 
Synthetic Signals Reproduce Decoding Improvements




We test whether improvements from jointly decoding words require
neural information. (a)
 Each point is a word with accuracy plotted against the
standard deviation of its duration across training occurrences. (b)
 We test whether the decoder predicts words whose typical durations match the test occurrence. A three-second window can nevertheless contain neural responses to subsequent
words. We examine whether the predictability of this
