We presented 
RSIGame
, an autonomous agentic game development framework that formulates game creation as a recursive self-improvement process. 
RSIGame
 strengthens the development loop with broad exploration, structured diagnosis, prioritized improvement, and an evolving checklist that continuously expands the set of identified issues and improvement opportunities. Its local explore-diagnose-improve loop enables evidence-grounded revision of the executable game, while the global loop tracks long-horizon progress, preserves the best checkpoint, and detects saturation or regression. We further introduced training-based experience internalization to transfer successful development trajectories back into the backbone game generation model, improving future game creation beyond test-time refinement alone.
