This paper studies host-side overhead in PyTorch programs that invoke user-written Triton kernels. For short kernels, specialization management and host preparation outside compiled execution can dominate end-to-end latency. We propose 
Trident
, a Torch-MLIR-based compiler backend that addresses this cost with the 
