We proposed Neural Harmonic Measure Operator (NHMO), the first neural operator built explicitly around the harmonic measure, the canonical probability distribution from potential theory that mediates all solutions of the Dirichlet Laplace problem on a fixed domain. For Poisson source terms, the classical balayage decomposition extends the same harmonic measure to handle sources via a learned lift network with a zero-boundary gauge. Our framework reduces an end-to-end neural-operator problem to two coupled components: the boundary kernel 
