While the improvements across these classes are driven largely by the GNN’s ability to separate bright land from water, the performance differences that remain are themselves informative about the underlying pixel characteristics. The two near-shore classes perform worst, likely because some of their pixels are located along shorelines rather than being tied solely to bright land misclassification, which makes them intrinsically harder to classify. Based on the reasonably strong F1 score of 0.71 for the 
